0:00:01.000,0:00:05.720
The next step in the project is
sealing the wood. For this

0:00:05.720,0:00:10.679
operation, we prepare a small amount of
resin, which we apply with the help of

0:00:10.679,0:00:14.360
a brush over the entire surface of
the wood.

0:00:14.360,0:00:17.960
It is very important to cover
all exposed areas as thoroughly as possible and to

0:00:17.960,0:00:22.080
work the resin into the walls of
cavities, cracks, and all

0:00:22.080,0:00:27.800
voids present in the material. The main
purpose of this step is to

0:00:27.800,0:00:33.280
reduce as much as possible the formation
of air bubbles during the pour. Without

0:00:33.280,0:00:38.760
proper sealing, the air trapped in the pores
and cavities of the wood can be released

0:00:38.760,0:00:43.440
gradually into the resin. These bubbles do not
always appear in the first minutes after

0:00:43.440,0:00:48.199
pouring. In many situations, they may
continue to appear for several hours,

0:00:48.199,0:00:51.879
including when we are no longer near
the project to

0:00:51.879,0:00:57.120
notice and remove them in time. For this
reason, sealing the wood is one of the

0:00:57.120,0:01:01.320
steps that directly influence
the quality of the final result and should not

0:01:01.320,0:01:05.880
be treated lightly.
When using resins designed

0:01:05.880,0:01:10.000
for deep pours, the chances that
small bubbles will dissipate on their own are

0:01:10.000,0:01:14.880
very high. Even so, proper
sealing remains one of the

0:01:14.880,0:01:19.320
most effective methods of preventing
problems before

0:01:19.320,0:01:22.920
they have a chance to appear.
